WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
(festive music)

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.941
- All right, Henry, come on in!

00:00:05.941 --> 00:00:07.810
- Ready!
- Okay, Henry.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.480
Happy Holidays!

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.000
As people can probably
tell, we're celebrating

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.075
the holidays a little early.
(bells ringing)

00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:13.908
- Oh yes.

00:00:13.908 --> 00:00:17.160
- Oh yes, because we wanna
spread a little Christmas cheer

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.727
because you have a new
holiday movie coming out.

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:20.570
- I do.
- So, I thought we'd celebrate

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.414
with a good old-fashioned
game of Nog Pong.

00:00:23.414 --> 00:00:25.320
(festive music)

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.153
We're keeping it classy.
- Oh my God.

00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:28.550
I don't think I've even
played regular Pong.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.580
- [Kelly] Really, you've never?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.413
- [Henry] Yeah.
- I think I've only

00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:31.246
played it once.

00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:32.220
- [Henry] Really?
- And I didn't win,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.053
I'll tell you that.
- [Henry] Okay.

00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:33.973
- Then I don't remember
the rest of the night.

00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:34.806
(laughs)

00:00:34.806 --> 00:00:35.933
- We'll be as bad as
each other, It's fine!

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:36.766
- [Kelly] It's really bad.

00:00:36.766 --> 00:00:37.640
(festive music)

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.520
We are just missing
one crucial ingredient!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.344
I'm gonna pour a tiny
bit just in all of 'em.

00:00:42.344 --> 00:00:43.324
- Right, so you're spiking?

00:00:43.324 --> 00:00:44.157
Holy moly.

00:00:44.157 --> 00:00:44.990
- Okay, I am.
- Got it.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.232
- Watch this Henry, this
is how we do it in Te-has.

00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:48.450
- [Henry] Aye!

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.970
- [Kelly] This is how you do it in Te-has!

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.260
- Good lord!

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.819
- This is why I don't remember the night!

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:55.690
(laughs)

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.160
Okay, the rules are simple,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.797
you toss a ball into one of my cups.

00:00:58.797 --> 00:00:59.630
- [Henry] Yeah.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.020
- [Kelly] And I have to drink
and vice versa, you got it?

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.853
- Got it.

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:04.445
- Okay and what we're playing
for, so glad you asked.

00:01:04.445 --> 00:01:05.610
(laughs)

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.870
The winner gets to go
home with a highly coveted

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:11.124
first annual Nog Pong
World Championship belt!

00:01:11.124 --> 00:01:13.835
- [Henry] Oh my God, look at that thing!

00:01:13.835 --> 00:01:16.502
(angelic music)

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:21.930
- Let's take positions,
are you ready to start?

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:22.763
- Ladies first.

00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:23.596
- Okay, well I'm gonna ask a question

00:01:23.596 --> 00:01:24.429
while we're doing this.
- [Henry] All right,

00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:25.262
go for it.
- 'Cause I'm trying

00:01:25.262 --> 00:01:26.161
to throw you off your game, okay.

00:01:26.161 --> 00:01:27.119
(laughs)

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:27.952
- You won't need to.

00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:30.200
- What is Last Christmas about?

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.740
'Cause I'm excited.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.310
Oh shoot.
- Oh.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.370
- Oh good, I love it, I
love it, I'm using yours.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:38.490
- Emilia Clarke's character
Kate, want to be a singer.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.323
- Oh!

00:01:39.323 --> 00:01:40.970
- She's kind of having
that quarter-life crisis

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.510
that we all, sort of,
often get ourselves into

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.260
and she meets a young man called Tom

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.450
who gives her a different
perspective on life

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.690
and there's George Michael music.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.141
- George Michael, I'm in!

00:01:52.141 --> 00:01:52.974
- Sold!

00:01:52.974 --> 00:01:54.081
- We suck.

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:54.914
(bell ding)

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:55.747
- [Both] Oh!

00:01:55.747 --> 00:01:56.639
- You spoke too soon!

00:01:56.639 --> 00:01:58.686
(sigh)

00:01:58.686 --> 00:01:59.757
- Everything is fine.

00:01:59.757 --> 00:02:00.753
(laughing)

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.070
- The juice!

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:02.903
- I love this though,
(bell ding)

00:02:02.903 --> 00:02:03.870
I'm excited to see this movie.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.772
I'm also excited to get D-runk!

00:02:05.772 --> 00:02:06.605
(laughs)

00:02:06.605 --> 00:02:07.850
Whoa!

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:08.683
Okay.

00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:09.516
- How well does that go down?

00:02:09.516 --> 00:02:11.094
- It's so, there's a lot of bourbon.

00:02:11.094 --> 00:02:12.377
- [Henry] It's good!

00:02:12.377 --> 00:02:13.210
(bell ding)

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.967
- Yes!
- [Henry] Ah.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.800
(bell ding)

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.030
- Where did you grow up?

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:22.110
- I grew up, I split time
between Malaysia and the UK.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:22.943
So Surrey.
- Oh.

00:02:22.943 --> 00:02:26.560
- So, from 10 onwards, I was in the UK.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.393
- [Kelly] Oh, right on.

00:02:27.393 --> 00:02:28.660
- So those are the best years
of, like, Christmas presents.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.070
- Yeah, I love the UK, God

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:32.010
and anytime you're in
England at Christmas time,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.328
it's more magical.

00:02:33.328 --> 00:02:34.161
(festive music)

00:02:34.161 --> 00:02:35.880
So what is your favorite Christmas movie?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.410
I'll go first, White Christmas.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:38.310
- Elf is ex--

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.143
- Nailed it!
(bell ding)

00:02:39.143 --> 00:02:40.130
- Ah.
- Yes!

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.740
I am like, I am--

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.573
- Damn!

00:02:43.573 --> 00:02:45.100
- So good!

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.650
What was your job before acting?

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.243
- Oh, I used to work in
a salon doing blowouts,

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.492
cuts, drys, men hair, color.
- What?

00:02:55.492 --> 00:02:56.480
Does your wife just love you?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.391
Does she have you do that?

00:02:57.391 --> 00:02:58.440
- More often than not,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.524
I'm doing her hair for
whenever we're on a red carpet

00:03:00.524 --> 00:03:01.357
- I love it!

00:03:01.357 --> 00:03:03.957
- And you see my wife, like
I usually do the blowout.

00:03:03.957 --> 00:03:04.923
- Oh my gosh!

00:03:04.923 --> 00:03:06.183
What was your specialty?
(bell ding)

00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:07.016
When you're a hairdresser.

00:03:07.016 --> 00:03:07.849
You're kinda nailing this at this point.

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:08.691
- Aye.

00:03:08.691 --> 00:03:09.524
- [Kelly] That's mine.

00:03:09.524 --> 00:03:11.630
- It was kind of that
Chelsea, waves blowout

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.120
which was like, big and
voluminous and sexy.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.240
- I'm gonna want you
to do that to my hair.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.122
- Absolutely, any time you need me!

00:03:17.122 --> 00:03:19.029
- I'm like, oh!
- Oh.

00:03:19.029 --> 00:03:19.912
(festive music)

00:03:19.912 --> 00:03:20.745
(bell ding)

00:03:20.745 --> 00:03:21.578
Oh, that's pretty good!

00:03:21.578 --> 00:03:23.444
- You know it, I am a woman of my word.

00:03:23.444 --> 00:03:24.353
- Really, oh, do you?

00:03:24.353 --> 00:03:25.523
Nah, you're a trooper.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.323
Oh lord.

00:03:27.323 --> 00:03:29.910
- You're kinda kicking
my behind at this game.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:30.997
- I got one last one as well.

00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:31.830
- Oh, shoot.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.860
- If I get this last one,

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.430
you have to do whatever row it land on.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.263
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:35.263 --> 00:03:36.096
- [Henry] The row.

00:03:36.096 --> 00:03:36.929
- I'm done, I'm done,

00:03:36.929 --> 00:03:38.603
don't you challenge me with a good time!

00:03:39.664 --> 00:03:40.497
(cartoon bounce)

00:03:40.497 --> 00:03:41.330
- [Henry] Oh!
- Ah!

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.163
- [Henry] Dang!
- You know what?

00:03:42.163 --> 00:03:42.996
You were closest to this
- [Henry] Yeah.

00:03:42.996 --> 00:03:43.829
- And I'll just do it.

00:03:43.829 --> 00:03:45.069
(laughing)

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:46.705
- Jeez!

00:03:46.705 --> 00:03:47.538
- Congrats!

00:03:47.538 --> 00:03:50.013
You are the first Egg
Nog Pong World Champion!

00:03:50.013 --> 00:03:50.930
- Aye, woo woo woo!

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.030
- I mean, you kind of,

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.360
I think baited me a bit

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.850
and said you weren't really good and this

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:56.590
and then kind of killed me.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.423
It's fine.

00:03:57.423 --> 00:03:58.256
- I might have played a couple times.

00:03:58.256 --> 00:03:59.210
Come on, come on.
- Do you want me to put it on?

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.390
Here we go.
- Of course I do.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.223
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:01.223 --> 00:04:02.056
- I'm walking out with this,
what are you talking about?

00:04:02.056 --> 00:04:03.720
- [Kelly] It's sticking on my sweater.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.386
- This is only coming
back next when you guys,

00:04:05.386 --> 00:04:06.480
(laughs)

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.250
when I do another Christmas movie.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.381
(camera snaps)

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:11.140
(crowd applauding)

